;; -*- mode: fundamental; coding: utf-8 -*-
;; SKK-JISYO.kei - the supplement of Kei's input method, looked in before SKK-JISYO.X.
;;
;; Copyright (C) 2026 Awe Morris
;; SPDX-License-Identifier: Zlib
;;
;; An original work written for Kei (WS095, decision D3): about a thousand
;; everyday words that REmacs's SKK-JISYO.X lacks or orders for other texts,
;; pronouns, greetings, time and counters, family, basic nouns, loanwords of
;; daily life and of computing, and the basic verbs and adjectives.  No entry
;; is copied from another dictionary.  Widened from the 337 headwords of
;; ws095-p003 in ws095-p012; plan/ws095/tests/ja-heldout.tsv was written and
;; frozen before the widening and is not used to choose words.
;;
;; Where a word is usually written in kana, the kana come first; of words read
;; alike, the one more common in daily writing comes first.
;;
;; Verbs and adjectives are written with every kana that does not change in
;; the candidate, and an SKK annotation that names how the candidate
;; conjugates, which the engine reads (ja-dict.c, ja-inflect.c):
;;
;;   五段    the headword's letter is the row of the kana that conjugates
;;           (読む よm /読;五段/, 終わる おわr /終わ;五段/);
;;   一段    the headword's letter is the r of る, and the endings follow the
;;           candidate (食べる たべr /食べ;一段/);
;;   形容詞  the headword's letter is the i or k of い or く, and the endings
;;           follow the candidate (新しい あたらしi /新し;形容詞/).
;;
;; The lines stay SKK's: an SKK input method shows the candidate, without its
;; annotation, before the okurigana typed (TabeRu gives 食べる).  A reading
;; shared by a godan and an ichidan verb lists both (かえr: 帰ります, 変えます).
;; The verbs usually written in kana (いる, ある, なる, できる) are the
;; engine's own and are not listed.
;;
;; okuri-ari entries.
